# Which Karabiner DriverKit VirtualHIDDevice package each kanata minor version needs, as
# kanata minor | driver version | package URL | sha256.
#
# Kanata types through the virtual keyboard this driver provides, and the two speak one IPC
# protocol that changes between driver majors, so a kanata built for one driver cannot talk to
# the daemon of another. This table is the pin for both. It is the one place either version is
# written, the way lazy-lock.json is for Neovim, and src/setup-kanata.sh reads it and nothing
# else. The installed kanata picks its row by its minor version, and the step refuses to go on
# when there is none.
#
# A new row is written before an upgrade, from kanata's own release notes, with the URL of the
# package on the driver's GitHub release and the sha256 that release lists for it, and then
# committed. `src/setup-kanata.sh --upgrade` stops until the row for Homebrew's stable kanata is
# here. decisions/kanata.md has the pairing as measured and where each answer came from.

# kanata | driver | package                                                                                                                     | sha256
1.12     | 6.2.0  | https://github.com/pqrs-org/Karabiner-DriverKit-VirtualHIDDevice/releases/download/v6.2.0/Karabiner-DriverKit-VirtualHIDDevice-6.2.0.pkg | 9e8c46239f0748161241e42444857901224e5c82f5b58a1731df4c70bf0736a8
